    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support from Australia through the Transparency International Indo-Pacific Partnership (TI IPP) Program Phase 2 has enabled Transparency International (TI) Solomon Islands to deliver a targeted information session on the Constituency Development Fund (CDF) Act 2023 for members of the West &#x2018;Are&#x2019;Are Rokotanikeni Association (WARA), the country&#x2019;s largest women&#x2019;s saving group.
&#x200d;
The CDF Act aims to improve the management and transparency of local development funds (CDFs), which have long been vulnerable to misuse and political interference. The session equipped women, including participants with disabilities, with practical knowledge and tools to engage in upcoming constituency consultations with community members and local chiefs. By demystifying how CDFs are meant to function, the initiative ensured participants could engage confidently on anti-corruption concerns and strengthen social accountability within their constituencies. This effort was enabled by the TI IPP Program Phase 2, DFAT&#x2019;s principal regional anti-corruption investment helping to empower citizens to demand transparent, accountable governance and reduce corruption risks.</narrative>
    </description>
