    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Under the Transparency International Indo-Pacific Partnership (TI IPP) Program Phase 2, Australia supported Transparency International (TI) Vanuatu to strengthen the implementation of the Right to Information Act by embedding transparency practices in public institutions. Through sustained advocacy the chapter worked with the Public Service Commission (PSC) to train and appoint 20 Right to Information (RTI) focal officers across 13 government ministries &#x2013; laying practical foundations for citizens to access information and hold government departments to account.  
&#x200d;
 In parallel, TI Vanuatu supported the Office of the Ombudsman to review its corporate plan to improve operational efficiency. As a result, the Ombudsman requested and successfully secured an increased operational budget to better fulfil its mandate. The additional funding will support the re-establishment of an office in Luganville, Santo, and expanded awareness-raising activities in rural areas in 2025. Together these steps are helping to strengthen public sector transparency and responsiveness, ensuring the RTI framework in Vanuatu is not only legislated but actively implemented. Advancements like these are central to the TI IPP Program Phase 2, DFAT&#x2019;s principal regional anti-corruption investment promoting accountable governance and active citizen engagement to reduce corruption across the Indo-Pacific.</narrative>
    </description>
