    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">With Australian support through the Transparency International Indo-Pacific Partnership (TI IPP) Program Phase 2, Transparency International (TI) Indonesia has advanced disability inclusion in Indonesia&#x2019;s national procurement processes. Through its three-day Youth Integrity Bootcamp, the chapter mobilised 28 young people from seven provinces, including youth with disabilities, to monitor procurement practices and advocate for inclusive governance. Training covered procurement stages, corruption risk identification and mitigation, budget management strategies and good practice monitoring for public procurement activities.  Equipped with these skills, participants monitored major national programs, including critical infrastructure projects and advocated for disability-inclusive provisions. The trained youth also submitted findings and recommendations to the National Public Procurement Agency (LKPP). This led to the LKPP adopting significant accessibility improvements including guideways, braille signage and voice-enabled websites that will help ensure government services are more inclusive. 
&#x200d;
TI Indonesia&#x2019;s continued advocacy also prompted LKPP to reintroduce structured civil society engagement in its 2025 Strategic Plan, embedding inclusive governance practice into the future.   Through the TI IPP Program Phase 2 &#x2013; Australia&#x2019;s principal regional anti&#x2013;corruption development investment &#x2013; TI is strengthening inclusive, accountable procurement systems and amplifying local civic voices in the Indo Pacific.</narrative>
    </description>
