    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">With support from Australia through the Transparency International Indo-Pacific Partnership (TI IPP) Program Phase 2, Transparency International (TI) Pakistan carried out its 2024 Transparency in Corporate Reporting Assessment, reviewing the public disclosures of companies listed on the Pakistan Stock Exchange. Using TI&#x2019;s globally recognised methodology, the assessment examined corporate transparency in relation to anti-corruption practices, human rights and Environmental, Social and Corporate Governance commitments. 
&#x200d;
Based on these results, TI Pakistan issued recommendations to companies and regulatory bodies, including the Securities and Exchange Commission of Pakistan to strengthen corporate governance frameworks and encourage sustainable, ethical and climate-responsible business operations. Delivered through the TI IPP Phase 2, DFAT&#x2019;s principal regional anti-corruption investment, this work is helping build more transparent markets and stronger regulatory oversight across Pakistan&#x2019;s corporate sector.</narrative>
